      "SettingsPatch": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Partial Settings for PATCH /api/settings.\n\nEvery field is Optional and \"unset\" (not just None) means \"leave as\nis\" -- SettingsStore.patch() checks `model_fields_set`, not `is None`,\nfor every field except leader_overrides, where None is the documented\n\"clear this leader's override\" sentinel.\n\nRange constraints (ge/le, max_length) are intentionally NOT duplicated\nhere. contracts.models.Settings is the single source of truth for\nvalid ranges; SettingsStore.patch() re-validates the merged result\nthrough it before writing, which still 422s a bad value, just one\nlayer later, with the file-untouched guarantee coming from\nvalidate-then-write ordering in SettingsStore.patch().",
        "properties": {
          "contract_version": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Contract Version"
          },
          "daily_loss_limit_usd": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
